# kk: Route presentation through Metal3 due to window server crash
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/43491 state=closed
# ### What does this MR do and why?
<!-- Describe in detail what your merge request does and why. -->

Ugly hack, but at least we don't crash the whole window system logging out users. I'm pretty sure this is an OS bug but haven't added the workaround flag for now since I'd like to investigate a little further (and Apple seems to be quite responsive with the report on this one). Maybe we can roll this back eventually.

```
kk: Route present through Metal3 to avoid window server crash
    
If we use Metal4 for presentation the window server will crash with faster
GPUs such as M4 Max or M5 Pro. The reason it's not well understood but all
points to a Metal bug. This commit routes the presentation command through
Metal3 which doesn't have the mentioned crash
    
Signed-off-by: Aitor Camacho <aitor@lunarg.com>
```

```
wsi/metal: Flag to understand if WSI needs to call present on drawable

Signed-off-by: Aitor Camacho <aitor@lunarg.com>
```
